at the heart of this case is a chatty  nosey little girl  who her family say was nine  going on 19.  in their first statement they said liv  was adored by everyone who knew her and  would instantly make friends with anyone  and everyone  she was often seen going up and down the  street on her new bike she'd just got  for her birthday  although her life was short her  personality certainly wasn't and she  lived it to the most she could and would  blow people away with her wit and  kindness  we as a family are heartbroken and have  lost a huge part of our life  if anyone knows anything  now is the time to speak up  it is not about being a snitch or a  grass  it is about finding who took our baby  away from us  please  do the right thing  her mum cheryl is now out of hospital  and is being supported by the police who  have started one of their biggest ever  manhunts  after the shooting here at the top of  the screen on a neighbour's cctv we see  a flash of feet running away from the  scene  detectives have only been able to say  that he was dressed in black with a  balaclava five foot seven inches tall  and slim build  they have been given names but still  don't have their prime suspect  my message to him remains the same  we will not rest until we find you  and we will find you  how confident are you that he is still  in this city or still in the northwest  of england  it doesn't really matter to me we will  find him wherever he goes we have proved  that time and time again within multiple  inquiries could he be out of the country  then it's unclear at this stage i can't  comment any further  information is still flowing into them  progress they say is being made in this  and the two other fatal shootings that  merseyside police are investigating  but it's never as fast as everyone would  like  it takes time and patience to build  these kinds of cases but ultimately it  will count for very little if they can't  find the gunman who killed olivia  the requests for help are echoing around  the city  our entire community needs to come  together  if you know anything or have any  information on the incident please let  the authorities know  keeping quiet is not an option enough is  enough  quite simply olivia's family need  answers for them  doing what's right  could mean everything  tom parmenter sky news liverpool
 

